---
export const prerender = true;

import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import ImageCompressor from '../../components/tools/ImageCompressor.astro';
import { imageCompressorVariants } from '../../data/variants/image-compressor';
import '../../styles/global.css';

const pageUrl = 'https://toolgearz.github.io/tools/image-compressor';
const faqs = [
  {
    question: 'Are my images uploaded while compressing them?',
    answer: 'No. The selected files are decoded and compressed with your browser’s image and Canvas APIs. The tool does not upload files to a server or call an image API.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Which image types and output formats are supported?',
    answer: 'You can select JPG/JPEG, PNG, and WebP files. Output can be JPEG or WebP. This Canvas workflow does not provide lossless PNG output, so PNG inputs are converted to the chosen format.',
  },
  {
    question: 'Can the compressor reach an exact target size?',
    answer: 'It tries a range of quality settings toward your target. Some images cannot reach a requested size without excessive quality loss; the result displays a warning and the actual file size.',
  },
  {
    question: 'How many images can I process at once?',
    answer: 'Up to 20 files can be processed per selection. Each file must be 40 MB or smaller, and decoded images are limited to 40 megapixels for browser memory safety.',
  },
];
const webApplicationSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'WebApplication',
  name: 'Image Compressor',
  url: pageUrl,
  applicationCategory: 'MultimediaApplication',
  operatingSystem: 'Any',
  browserRequirements: 'Requires JavaScript and Canvas support',
  offers: { '@type': 'Offer', price: '0', priceCurrency: 'USD' },
};
const faqSchema = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@type': 'FAQPage',
  mainEntity: faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => ({
    '@type': 'Question',
    name: question,
    acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: answer },
  })),
};
const toolDefaults = {
  quality: 80,
  outputFormat: 'image/webp' as const,
  lockFormat: false,
};
const toolLabels = {
  title: 'Compress images in your browser',
  description: 'Adjust quality, set an optional target size, resize, compare previews, and download optimized images. Your files stay on your device.',
  fileHelp: 'Drop or choose JPG, PNG, or WebP · up to 20 files, 40 MB each',
  targetHelp: 'Optional: compression tries lower quality values to reach this size, but some images cannot meet a very small target.',
  privacyNote: 'Images are processed locally. Each file is limited to 40 MB and 40 megapixels to avoid excessive browser memory use.',
};
---

<Layout
  title="Image Compressor | Compress JPG, PNG & WebP Locally | ToolGearz"
  description="Compress JPG, PNG, and WebP images in your browser. Adjust quality, resize, target a file size, compare previews, and download without uploading images."
  url="/tools/image-compressor"
  analytics={false}
>
  <Navbar />
  <main class="mx-auto w-[min(1000px,calc(100%-2rem))] pb-12">
    <header class="py-12 sm:py-16">
      <a href="/tools" class="text-sm font-bold text-teal-800 hover:text-teal-950">← All tools</a>
      <p class="mb-2 mt-7 text-xs font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-teal-800">Design &amp; developer tools · Runs in your browser</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-950 sm:text-4xl">Image Compressor</h1>
      <p class="mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-7 text-slate-600">Reduce image file sizes, optionally resize, compare previews, and download optimized images. Your files stay on your device.</p>
    </header>

    <ImageCompressor defaults={toolDefaults} labels={toolLabels} />

    <article class="mt-10 space-y-5 leading-7 text-slate-700">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">Choose dimensions before sacrificing quality</h2>
        <p>Image compression reduces the bytes needed to store or transfer a picture. JPEG and quality-based WebP settings trade some fine visual detail for smaller files; the useful balance depends on the image and where it will be displayed. Resizing can provide an additional reduction when a camera image has many more pixels than its display area needs. This browser tool uses the Canvas encoder, so there is no remote image service or upload queue.</p>
        <p>Select multiple JPEG, PNG, or WebP source images, set an output format and quality, and optionally enter maximum width, height, or target kilobytes. Dimensions preserve aspect ratio and act as upper bounds: smaller originals are not enlarged. If a target is set, the encoder tests lower quality settings to approach it, then reports the actual output size. A clear warning appears if the target cannot be reached.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">A careful compression workflow</h2>
        <ol class="list-decimal space-y-2 pl-6">
          <li>Check the destination’s file-size, format, and pixel-dimension rules before editing.</li>
          <li>Start from an original image and set maximum dimensions to match its intended display.</li>
          <li>Choose JPEG for an opaque photo or WebP when your workflow supports it; WebP can retain transparency.</li>
          <li>Compress and inspect the preview, actual dimensions, size, and warnings before downloading.</li>
        </ol>
        <p>Canvas re-encoding may discard metadata, animation, or color-profile details. Animated images are not preserved as animations. PNG inputs are converted to the selected JPEG or WebP format, not a lossless PNG. JPEG has no transparency, so transparent pixels are composited onto white. Keep an original when fidelity, transparency, or metadata matters.</p>
      </section>
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">Find a preset for a specific image task</h2>
        <p>Different upload forms and publishing workflows call for different size goals. The following pages open with dedicated settings and explain the trade-offs for that intent. Their values are starting points rather than universal platform requirements; check the receiving service before relying on a particular format or file limit.</p>
        <ul class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          {imageCompressorVariants.map((variant) => (
            <li>
              <a class="block rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-3 font-bold text-teal-800 hover:border-teal-400 focus-visible:outline focus-visible:outline-2 focus-visible:outline-offset-2 focus-visible:outline-teal-700" href={`/tools/image-compressor/${variant.slug}`}>
                {variant.heading}
              </a>
            </li>
          ))}
        </ul>
      </section>
      <section aria-labelledby="image-faq-heading">
        <h2 id="image-faq-heading" class="text-2xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">Frequently asked questions</h2>
        <div class="space-y-4">
          {faqs.map(({ question, answer }) => (
            <div>
              <h3 class="mb-1 text-lg font-bold text-slate-900">{question}</h3>
              <p class="mb-0">{answer}</p>
            </div>
          ))}
        </div>
      </section>
    </article>
    <section class="mt-8 rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 sm:p-7" aria-labelledby="image-related-heading">
      <h2 id="image-related-heading" class="text-xl font-extrabold text-slate-950">Related design tools</h2>
      <div class="grid gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
        <a class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-4 font-bold text-teal-800 hover:border-teal-400" href="/tools/svg-formatter">SVG Formatter</a>
        <a class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-4 font-bold text-teal-800 hover:border-teal-400" href="/tools/color-converter">Color Converter</a>
        <a class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 p-4 font-bold text-teal-800 hover:border-teal-400" href="/tools/css-minifier">CSS Minifier</a>
      </div>
    </section>
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(webApplicationSchema)} />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
  </main>
  <Footer />
</Layout>
